# This project's paths that no check reads, on top of the stack's in
# .github/gate-checks/gateignore: the Gate workflow skips the checks of a PR that changes only
# listed paths. The patterns are .gitignore's, read after the stack's, so a later pattern wins
# and a `!` pattern runs the checks on a path the stack lists. As in .gitignore, a `!` can't put
# back a file inside a folder that a pattern matches: write a folder as `dir/**`, and put back
# its subfolders with `!dir/**/` before a file in one of them. The Gate reads this file as the
# PR's base has it, so a change here applies to the PRs after the one that makes it.
# Each pattern takes its reason on the `#` lines directly above it, in the form
# .claude/rules/conventions.md gives under Skipped checks.
